Requirement Analysis Phase
The Requirement Analysis Phase defines what the ServiceNow ACL lab must accomplish before any configuration is performed. The main objective is to translate the security requirement—users should access Institution Details records according to their roles and the Branch field value—into clear functional, security, and validation requirements.

1. Business Requirement
The organization maintains student/institution records in a custom ServiceNow table named u_institution_details.

Each record contains a Branch value such as:

ECE

EEE

CSE

The organization requires branch-based record-level security. In this lab, EEE users should be able to access EEE records, while users without the required role should not be able to access the records.

Administrators must retain unrestricted access.

The access model is progressively expanded using four custom roles:

Role	Purpose	Required Operation
bb1	EEE record access	Read
bb2	Create records	Create
bb3	Modify records	Write
bb4	Remove records	Delete
admin	Administrative access	All operations

2. User Requirements
A test user must be created to validate the ACL behavior.

Test user:

User ID: EEE User

First Name: EEE

Last Name: User

Email: eeeuser@gmail.com

The user will be assigned the custom roles required for testing.

Initially, the lab creates:

bb1

bb2

bb3

bb4

The roles represent different levels of access rather than being treated as a single permission.

3. Role-Based Access Requirements
The access requirements should be clearly separated by operation.

Read requirement
A user must have the bb1 role to read Institution Details records.

For the intended business rule:

A non-admin user with bb1 should be permitted to access EEE records.

Users without bb1 should not be able to read the protected records.

Administrators with the admin role must be able to read all records regardless of Branch.

Create requirement
A user must have bb2 to create a new Institution Details record.

The create ACL does not require a Branch data condition according to the lab specification.

Therefore, the create permission is controlled primarily by the user's role.

Write requirement
A user must have bb3 to modify an existing record.

The intended combined access model is:

bb1 + bb3

This allows the user to access the records through the read ACL and modify permitted records through the write ACL.

Delete requirement
A user must have bb4 to delete a record.

The intended complete access model is:

bb1 + bb2 + bb3 + bb4

This allows the test user to read, create, modify, and delete records subject to the configured ACLs.

